Using VC APPS Protocol Analyzer to Dump Transactions From
Custom VIP
The VC APPs Protocol Analyzer provides an interface to integrate third-party VIPs into
the Verdi environment. The objective of this feature is to standardize the Verdi Protocol
Analyzer. It serves as the common debug platform for Synopsys VIPs and third-party
VIPs. This interface supports the components that can generate both simple and complex
(hierarchical) protocol-style transactions.
The Verdi Protocol Analyzer uses protocol-specific data stored in a common FSDB
database. It also uses protocol knowledge from the Synopsys VIP. The tool creates a
high-level, interactive display with protocol analysis and debug capabilities. To integrate
third-party VIPs into Verdi, you must capture protocol-specific activity. You must also
store that data in an FSDB. You must have access to the VIP source code to capture
the protocol-specific activities. You must also specify the protocol information needed for
protocol-specific debug features in Verdi. The protocol specification defines the activity
that occurs in each layer. It also defines each layer's associated data. It defines how data
communicates between the layers.

