One-Hot Encoding

One-Hot Encoding
State-encoding is the way in which binary numbers are assigned to states. The different
state encoding formats commonly used are sequential, gray, johnson, one-hot, and defineyour-own. The Verdi platform supports sequential, gray, johnson, and one-hot. However,
one-hot is written in a different manner than the other formats. An example of Verilog onehot format is as follows:
one-hot state-encoding formatstate-encodingone-hot

module prep3 (clk, rst, in, out) ;
input clk, rst ;
input [7:0] in ;
output [7:0] out ;
parameter [2:0]
START = 0 ,
SA
= 1 ,
SB
= 2 ,
SC
= 3 ,
SD
= 4 ,
SE
= 5 ,
SF
= 6 ,
SG
= 7 ;
reg [7:0] state, next_state ;
reg [7:0] out, next_out ;
always @ (in or state) begin
// default values
next_state = 8'b0 ;
next_out = 8'bx ;
case (1'b1) // synopsys parallel_case full_case
state[START]:
if (in == 8'h3c) begin
next_state[SA] = 1'b1 ;
next_out = 8'h82 ;
end
else begin
next_state[START] = 1'b1 ;
next_out = 8'h00 ;
end
state[SA]:
case (in) // synopsys parallel_case full_case
8'h2a:
next_state[SC] = 1'b1 ;
next_out = 8'h40 ;
end
8'h1f:
next_state[SB] = 1'b1 ;
next_out = 8'h20 ;
end
default:
next_state[SA] = 1'b1 ;
next_out = 8'h04 ;
end

One-Hot Encoding

state[SB]:
if (in == 8'haa) begin
next_state[SE] = 1'b1 ;
next_out = 8'h11 ;
end
else begin
next_state[SF] = 1'b1 ;
next_out = 8'h30 ;
end
state[SC]:
next_state[SD] = 1'b1 ;
next_out = 8'h08 ;
end
state[SD]:
next_state[SG] = 1'b1 ;
next_out = 8'h80 ;
end
state[SE]:
next_state[START] = 1'b1 ;
next_out = 8'h40 ;
end
state[SF]:
next_state[SG] = 1'b1 ;
next_out = 8'h02 ;
end
state[SG]:
