NPI FSDB Time-Based VC Iterator
Traversing FSDB values in a time-based way is the most commonly used application.

npiFsdbTimeBasedVcIter::add
Add a signal to the iterator.
All signals added to the iterator must be from the same FSDB file handle).

NPI_INT64 add( npiFsdbSigHandle sig )
NPI_INT64 add( npiFsdbSigHandle sig, NPI_UINT32 filterEq )

sig

An FSDB signal handle that is traversed later in this iterator.
filterEq

Indicates if filtering out equivalent signals (0: not filter, 1: filter).
On success, return a number greater than 0. (Note: when filterEq is 1, the return number
for equivalent signals is the same).
int main(int argc, char** argv) {
npiFsdbFileHandle fp = npi_fsdb_open( "novas.fsdb" );
npiFsdbSigHandle sigA = npi_fsdb_sig_by_name(fp, "top.U1.A", NULL);
npiFsdbSigHandle sigB = npi_fsdb_sig_by_name(fp, "top.U1.B", NULL);
npiFsdbTimeBasedVcIter vcIter;

if ( !vcIter.add( sigA ) )
printf("Error. Failed to add sigA.\n");
if ( !vcIter.add( sigB ) )
printf("Error. Failed to add sigB.\n");
vcIter.iter_start( 10000, 20000 );
while( vcIter.iter_next( vcTime, sig ) ) {
if ( !vcIter.get_value( val ) ) {
printf("Error. Failed to get value.\n");
}
if ( sig == sigA)
printf("sigA = %s at time %llu\n", val.value.str, vcTime);
printf("sigB = %s at time %llu\n", val.value.str, vcTime);
}
}

