npi_crdb_is_correlated
Checks whether input RTL and gate level objects are correlated.
If they are correlated, returns 1 and returns whether they are inversely mapped by
parameter polarity; otherwise, returns 0.
If they are inverse mapping, the polarity is 1; otherwise, the polarity is 0.
Users should check return value before using polarity value.

The input object of RTL and gate level should be both scopes or both signals.
Besides, they should be in the same CRDB.

npi_crdb_set_correlation - Sets the mapping between input RTL and gate level object
npi_crdb_unset_correlation - Breaks the mapping between input RTL and gate level

NPI_INT32 npi_crdb_is_correlated ( npiCrdbHandle database, npiCrdbHandle
rtl_sig_or_scope_hdl, npiCrdbHandle gate_sig_or_scope_hdl, NPI_INT32
*polarity/*O*/ );

npiCrdbHandle database

npiCrdbHandle rtl_sig_or_scope_hdl

npiCrdbHandle gate_sig_or_scope_hdl

NPI_INT32 *polarity/*O*/

Returns the polarity value of input RTL and gate level handles.
When input RTL and gate level object are inversely mapped, saves 1 to the memory
pointed by polarity; otherwise, saves 0.
Check return string before using this value.
If input RTL and Gate objects are correlated, returns 1; otherwise, returns 0.
NPI_INT32 code = 0;
NPI_INT32 polarity = 0; //init output
code = npi_crdb_is_correlated (crdbHandle, rtl_scope_handle,
gate_scope_handle, &polarity/*O*/);
if( code ) {
if( polarity )
printf ("They are inverse correlated.\n");

}

printf ("They are correlated.\n");

