Use
Use is a group that contains stmt, ports, cont-assign, prim-term, case-item, and mp-port.
Only simple-expr, part-select, and indexed-part-select can obtain use by applying method
npiUse. Use contains the object that overlaps the reference handle.

module mm(p);
input p;
bit [3:0] r; /* bit var */
mm m0(r[0]);
r[1:0] /* part select */ = 0; /* assignment */
r[2-:2] /* indexed part select */ = 0; /* assignment */
end

In the example code above, bit var "top.r" gets assignment "r[1:0] = 0;" and "r[2-:2] =
0;" by applying method npiUse. Part-select "top.r[1:0]" gets port "p" located at top.m0,
assignment "r[1:0] = 0" and assignment "r[2-:2] = 0".

* For vectors, the npiUse relationship accesses any use of the vector, the overlapped
part, the part-selects or bit-selects of the vector.
For the following example, if npiUse is applied for top.p[0][0][20:18], the result is
top.p[0][0], top.p[0][0].a, top.p[0][0].b[1].x, top.p[0][0][20] and top.p[0][0].a[0].

bit [1:0] x;
byte y;
} ps2;
logic [9:0] a;
ps2 [1:0] b;
} ps1;
ps1 [1:0] p [1:0];
p[0][0] = 0; // use of the vector
p[0][0].a = 0; // use of the overlapped part of the vector
p[0][0].b[1].x = 0; // use of the part-selects of the vector
p[0][0][20] = 0; // use of the bit-selects of the vector
p[0][0].a[0] = 0; // the same as above
p[0][0].a[1] = 0;
p[1][0][20] = 0;
p[1][1][20] = 0;
p[0][0][23:21] = 0;
p[0][0][17] = 0;
end

* For bit-selects, the npiUse relationship accesses any specific use of that bit, any use of
the parent vector, and any part-select that contains that bit.
* If the result obtained by the npiUserelationship is located at the sub statement of
an npiAssignment such as npiDelayControl or npiEventControl, the returned
statement object is npiAssignment.
tmp2 = p tmp1;

The obtained object type by applying npiUse for p is npiAssignment (tmp2 = #p
tmp1;), not npiDelayControl (#p).
* For the use method of npiRefObj, the result objects do not check overlapping with the
reference handle

