Root or component is the most important building component in VHDL. The NPI Libraries
Root-Component library packs a set of APIs to traverse and dump elements in a root or
The elements of a root or component are defined in the VHDL LRM.
In VHDL, a root or component generally contains the following building blocks:
* Entity.
* Architecture.
* Ports.
* Generics.
* Signals.

* Variables.
* Components.
* Generate scopes.
* Components in the generate scopes.
* Procedures.
* Functions.
* Process.
* Blocks.
* Concurrent signal assignments.
* Concurrent procedure calls.
* Concurrent asserts.
* Language interfaces.
The NPI Libraries Module Library provides the corresponding APIs to get the handles
(npiHandle) for each type of element in a Module so you can easily get the handles to
access those Module elements. The library also provides dump APIs for each type of
element.
The NPI Libraries Module library is written based on the based on the NPI Language

The NPI Misc. library provides a set of APIs that are hard to be classified. The following
categories are included in the Misc. Library:
* Communicate with Novas by Socket: Use the socket client to control the novas
executable (C/C++ only).
* Interprocess Communication with Socket Client: Use the socket client to do
interprocess communication (C/C++ only).
* Argument Parser: Facilitate processing the arguments passed into a C/C++ program
(argv) (C/C++ only).
* Universal Scope Name: Create a Universal Scope Name (USN) representation for
hierarchical scopes in SystemVerilog and VHDL.

Communicate with Novas by Socket
When users want to call Novas commands in their C/C++ program, the following APIs
fulfill such a requirement:
