proc npi_l1_fsdb_sig_by_property_sig_vec
sigHdlVec propStruct sigHdlVecResult

propStruct

The property structure. This is for users to set the querying constraint.
For tcl, the property structure is defined as tcl::list and the usage rule is as below.
* Specify the constraint prototype const char* in each the expression
* Append the this const char* in tcl list.
* Put this list into this API as one of the argument.
The prototype const char* for each constraint is as following.
"npiFsdbL1SigName: "
"npiFsdbL1Real: "
"npiFsdbL1MDA: "
"npiFsdbL1LeftRange: "
"npiFsdbL1RightRange: "
"npiFsdbL1RangeSize: "
"npiFsdbL1Direction: "
"npiFsdbL1AssertionType: "
"npiFsdbL1CompositeType: "

The target scope name which the signals belong to.
It queries from the top scope if this argument is set as NULL.
passSubScope

The Boolean value to decide if the sub-scopes must be considered or not.
If it is true, the signals in all sub-scopes are queried.
If false, only the signals under target scope can be queried.

If the constraint const char* is illegal, then it returns FALSE.
If the constraint const char* is legal, then it returns TRUE.
