npi_nl_hier_tree_trv_register_cb
Register callback function for npi_nl_hier_tree_trv.
The API npi_nl_hier_tree_trv_register_cb creates the association between user-defined
callback function/data and npi_nl_hier_tree_trv. Object types that can be iterated from
scope are allowed to register callback functions. The registered callback function is called
by npi_nl_hier_tree_trv when the corresponding object type is traversed.
Also refer to npi_nl_hier_tree_trv and npi_nl_hier_tree_trv_reset_cb.
The object (npiNlHandle) is passed as an argument to the callback function
and be released when the execution of callback function is done. If users want
to preserve the object, npi_nl_set_permanent_handle can be used to set the
object as "permanent".
