Filter npiNlHandles of a specific npiNlPortType from a vector.
The NPI Netlist API npi_nl_ut_filter_port_instport filters the npiNlPortType of all handles in
a specified vector (C++) or array (Tcl).
Filtering uses either a positive or negative list.
The filtered result is collected into another specified vector (C++) or array (Tcl).

typedef std::vector < int > intVec_t;

npi_nl_ut_filter_port_instport ( nlHdlVec_t& inHdlVec, nlHdlVec_t&
outHdlVec, intVec_t& typeVec, bool isKeep );

inHdlVec

Specify the reference to a STL vector of type npiNlHandle to be filtered.
outHdlVec

Specify the reference to a STL vector of type npiNlHandle after filtering.
typeVec

Specify the reference to a STL vector of type integer, with contents of npiNlPortTypes for
filtering.
isKeep

A Boolean value specifying whether to collect the handles to the outHdlVec whose
npiNlPortType is listed in the typeVec (true), or to filter out those matched handles and
collect the rest to the outHdlVec (false).
N/A
reg clk, sel, r1, r2, r3;
wire w1 = (sel) ? r1: r2;
r3 <= w1;
end

{
npiNlHandle sigHdl = NULL;

nlHdlVec_t outHdlVec;
intVec_t typeVec;
typeVec.push_back(npiNlClockPort);
typeVec.push_back(npiNlControlPort);
printf("Mux input instports, filter and keep Control port:\n");
sigHdl =
npi_nl_L1_handle_by_name((char*)"top.top:Always0SigOp0:3:3:Mux.OH_w1");
npi_nl_trace_driver_by_hdl2(sigHdl, hdlVec/*O*/);
