npi_ut_get_define_location
Get a vector of definition location information.
Since SystemVerilog allows cross-file definition, NPI provides an API
npi_ut_get_define_location to collect location information of source code where the
object is defined. The location information contains three elements: file name, begin line
number, and end line number. The API helps users ease-to-track definition location when
the source code of definition are distributed in several files.

int npi_ut_get_define_location ( npiHandle instHdl, locInfoVec_t&
locInfoVec/*O*/ );

instHdl

The handle to an instance. Only the definition of module, interface, package, and program
are supported.
locInfoVec

Specify the reference of the vector where the definition location information is collected.

The type-define "locInfoVec_t" is listed as follows:
struct locInfo_s {
string fileName; // file name of definition location
int beginLine; // begin line number
int endLine; // end line number
};
typedef std::vector < locInfo_s > locInfoVec_t;

The number of definition location.
The example demonstrates a special case that the definition of module "ip" are divided
into three files: prod2_ip.v, design.v, and top.v.
top.v
include "./design.v"
wire sig;

ifdef PROD1
include "prod1/prod1_ip.v"
include "prod2/prod2_ip.v"
wire sig2;

prod1/prod1_ip.v
module ip;
wire [31:0] data32;

prod2/prod2_ip.v
module ip;
wire [63:0] data64;

{

npi_init(argc ,argv);

npiHandle hdl = npi_handle_by_name("ip", NULL);
locInfoVec_t locVec;
int retVal = npi_ut_get_define_location(hdl, locVec/*O*/);
printf("Got %d location.\n", retVal);
for (locInfoVec_t::iterator it = locVec.begin(); it!=locVec.end();
it++) {
printf("%d:\n", ++i);
printf("File
: %s\n", (*it).fileName.c_str());
printf("Begin Line : %d\n", (*it).beginLine);
printf("End Line
: %d\n", (*it).endLine);
}

}

