npi_nl_ut_get_reset_default_value
Get the reset default value by the Q-instport handle of a flip-flop.
The NPI Netlist API npi_nl_ut_get_reset_default_value returns the reset default
value string in specified format of the input handle.

npi_nl_ut_get_reset_default_value ( npiNlHandle hdl,
npiNlFormat_e format = npiNlBinFormat );

hdl

Specify the format for the output value string. Available values are listed as follows:
(default: npiNlBinFormat).
npiNlBinFormat Binary format
npiNlHexFormat Hexadecimal format
npiNlOctFormat Octal format
npiNlDecFormat Decimal format

A string representing the reset default value of the input handle is returned. If no value is
obtained, return NULL.
logic clk, rstn;
logic q;
logic async_reset_by_1;
logic async_reset_by_2;
logic async_reset_by_3;
always @(posedge clk or negedge rstn) begin
if(~rstn) begin
async_reset_by_1 <= 'h1;
end
async_reset_by_1 <= q;
end
end
always @(posedge clk or posedge rstn) begin
if(rstn) async_reset_by_2 <= 'h2;
else async_reset_by_2 <= q;
end
always @(posedge clk or negedge rstn) begin
async_reset_by_3 <= (!rstn) ? 'h3 : q;
end
logic sync_reset_by_4;
logic sync_reset_by_5;

sync_reset_by_4 <= (~rstn) ? 'h4 : q;
end
if(rstn) begin
sync_reset_by_5 <= 'h5;
end
sync_reset_by_5 <= q;
end
end

